<title>USA: Chester, N.J., weighs privatizing utilities -- paper.</title>
<headline>Chester, N.J., weighs privatizing utilities -- paper.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chester, N.J., is examining offers from outside companies to operate the borough's water and sewer systems, the Star Ledger reported Tuesday.</p>
<p>At least three firms have submitted proposals to run the system, which just completed a $1.9 million sewer project to upgrade facilities.</p>
<p>Borough officials have estimated it would cost $4 million to extend water mains into the Morris County Municipal Utilities Authority's water supply.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
